      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The island’s first European discovery dates back to 1502, when Portuguese navigators first charted its coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.encontrailhadogovernador.com.br/ilha-do-governador/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1663 launch of the Galeão Padre Eterno, then the world’s largest ship, took place off Ilha do Governador’s coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.encontrailhadogovernador.com.br/ilha-do-governador/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The island connects to Rio de Janeiro by a bridge and hosts a naval air station and shipyards that have operated for centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Governador-Island",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
